{
 "slug": "test/measurement-codable",
 "about": "A saved measurement's own logic — the same cases in every edition. Every case is a classical guitar measurement (guitarType 'Classical', measurementType 'Classical Guitar') holding 'peaks' (id, frequency in Hz, magnitude in dB), the 'selected' peak ids (null: no selection saved — a legacy file; []: Select None) and mode 'overrides' (peak id → label). tapToneRatio: the measurement's ratio, f(Top) / f(Air) over the definitive peaks — 'expect' within 'ratioTolerance', or null for none; 'live' rows are also given to a live analyzer with the same peaks, selection and overrides, which must give the same ratio. modeLabels: the label each peak is written with, in peak order — and the label the measurement gives it for display (the Details pane's), which must be the same; 'storedLabels' are labels the file already carries. selectionHeal: the measurement written and read back — whether the read flags it healed, and the selection it holds; 'material' rows are a material measurement (a longitudinal snapshot, no guitar spectrum). Expected values are Swift's. snapshotBytes: the spectrum written as base64 'frequenciesData' / 'magnitudesData' — exact text — and read back to the same float32 values. decode: a 'file' (the .guitartap array) and the fields it must read to: measurementName, peakMinThreshold, sampleRate (null: unknown), the snapshot's frequencies and magnitudes, overrides (peak id → label, ids compared ignoring case; {} for none), peakCount, the first peak's pitchNote, annotationVisibilityMode. write: a 'file' read and written again by the edition's writer — the keys that must be 'present' and 'absent' (a key anywhere in the document; 'peaks[].modeLabel' on every peak), the exact number 'text' written for a key, and text the output 'contains' once compact. fixtures: the real files every edition carries — each read to the facts given (the first measurement's name, peak count, sample rate, whether it is a comparison, its override labels), each override naming a peak the file contains, written again with no legacy key and with the spectrum's 'frequenciesData' / 'magnitudesData' exactly as the file has them, and read back with the same peaks and spectrum. comparison: a 'file' holding a comparison record, read (and, with 'roundTrip', written by the edition's writer and read again); 'expect' — 'isComparison', 'healed' (the reading healed something and flags the record to be saved again), 'entries' (per entry, in order, the fields named: id, label, colorComponents, guitarType — null for none — peakCount, modePeakIds: the stored map, mode display name → peak id, ids compared ignoring case; or null for no entries), 'modeFrequency' (the first entry's stored modes read back as frequencies), 'absent' (keys the written document does not contain).",
